  "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Lanterns Underroot hand-painted 2D platformer TERRAIN sprite atlas. Rich painterly wood/stone/soil materials, selective crisp silhouettes, restrained brush texture, moss/earth palette with cool teal-blue shadows and warm muted edges. Strict SIDE-ON ORTHOGRAPHIC camera, flat collision tops, no perspective top faces. Exactly1024x1024 square canvas, FOUR equal columns and FOUR equal rows, exactly16equal256pxcells. ONE complete module PER CELL, fitting inside, no spanning. Reading order row-by-row as listed. Genuine alpha outside material and under floating modules, opaque material interiors. NO scenery, props, characters, floor, lamps, glows, shadows, lettering, gridlines, dividers or labels. Four-by-four source modules for64px export, prototype edges pending seam repair. Reusable broken ledge/endcap modules,not intactterrain and not separate scenery. Row1 broken stoneleftcap,crackedstone repeat,brokenstonerightcap,cracked isolated ledge. Row2 splinteredwoodleftcap,crackedwoodrepeat,splinteredwoodrightcap,brokenshortwoodledge. Row3 snappedrootleftcap,crackedrootrepeat,snappedrootrightcap,brokenisolatedrootledge. Row4 four compact debris terrainmodules:smallstonechunkgroup,planksplintergroup,brokenrootsegmentgroup,mixedsmallstonewooddebris. Eachcomplete module padded within cell,no spilled debris across boundaries. Damage clear but stable flatwalktops onrows1\u20133.",
